---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Read the terms and important limitations for using WorkoutMatch exercise information, calculators, local storage, and export features."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms' }]} />
  </div>

  <header class="narrow section-sm">
    <p class="eyebrow">Use of the website</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These terms describe the intended use and important limitations of
      WorkoutMatch. If you do not agree with them, do not use the site.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="narrow terms-content">
    <section>
      <h2>Educational use only</h2>
      <p>
        WorkoutMatch provides general educational and organizational information
        for adults. Workouts, exercise descriptions, movement filters,
        calculators, and progress summaries are not medical advice, diagnosis,
        treatment, rehabilitation, nutrition care, or professional supervision.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for deciding whether to use a feature, checking your
        surroundings and equipment, choosing an appropriate effort, and stopping
        when needed. See the
        <a href="/safety/">safety guidance</a> before exercising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Adults and excluded uses</h2>
      <p>
        The initial workout and calculator experience is intended for adults
        aged 20 and older. It is not built for children or teens, pregnancy or
        postpartum programming, injury rehabilitation, competitive-sport
        preparation, eating-disorder treatment, or emergency decision-making.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Estimates and generated content</h2>
      <p>
        Rule-based workouts depend on the inputs, exercise data, template rules,
        and available candidates. They cannot observe technique or know
        individual readiness. BMI is a screening calculation, BMR is an equation
        estimate rather than a measured metabolic rate, and TDEE adds subjective
        activity-factor assumptions. Results are not guaranteed to be accurate
        or suitable for a particular decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/methodology/">methodology and source limitations</a> before
        interpreting results.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Local data and exports</h2>
      <p>
        Saved workout information is stored in your browser when supported and
        when you choose to save it. Local data can be blocked, cleared,
        corrupted, or lost, and is not backed up or synchronized by
        WorkoutMatch. You are responsible for exported files and for reviewing
        an import before confirming it. Read the <a href="/privacy/"
          >privacy page</a
        > for the complete data boundary.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        The site may change, become unavailable, or contain errors. Features can
        depend on browser support, device settings, storage availability, and
        deployment configuration. Do not rely on WorkoutMatch as the only copy
        of important information or as an emergency service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Names, links, and site content</h2>
      <p>
        WorkoutMatch is a working product name; no trademark, company-name, or
        domain clearance is implied. External links are provided for source
        context and convenience. Their operators control their own content and
        privacy practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not misuse the site, attempt to interfere with its operation, or
        present its generated or editorial content as individualized clinical
        guidance. These terms do not remove rights that cannot lawfully be
        excluded in your jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms-content {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .terms-content section + section {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .terms-content p {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }
</style>
